        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0230" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg58"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/479</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Elkus</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 420</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received February 23.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith copy
                    and translation of a note from the Ottoman Foreign Office dated January 19,
                    1917, in which the Minister of Foreign Affairs recapitulates the attitude of the
                    Sublime Porte in view of the response of the Entente powers to the overtures of
                    peace which were made by the Central powers on December 12 last. The general
                    tenor of this note has already been made public.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abram I. Elkus</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d51-a1.xml" xpointer="d51-a1"/>
            </div>
